From: Mauro Ribeiro <mauro.ribeiro@hardkernel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2: add V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC to codec/profile CID map

The stateful HEVC pixfmt was missing from kV4L2CodecPixFmtToProfileCID
(only the stateless V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC_SLICE was listed), so
EnumerateSupportedProfilesForV4L2Codec returned empty for drivers like
Amlogic meson-vdec that expose stateful V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC. The renderer
SupplementalDecoderVideoProfileCache was never populated with HEVCMain
and FFmpegDemuxer rejected every HEVC stream as unsupported.

Signed-off-by: Mauro Ribeiro <mauro.ribeiro@hardkernel.com>
---
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
@@ -332,6 +332,7 @@
         {V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_PROFILE},
         {V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_PROFILE},
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_HEVC_PARSER_AND_HW_DECODER)
+        {V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_PROFILE},
         {V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC_SLICE, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_PROFILE},
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_HEVC_PARSER_AND_HW_DECODER)
         {V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP8, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_VP8_PROFILE},
